  "visual_observations": [
    "I inspected all five current actual LibreOffice renders after calibration and checked their render-source bindings. The Georgia titles now share a stable top origin and apparent size. The Arial subtitle line and neutral divider remain steady as the page content changes.",
    "The wide pale-orange decision bands now hold a fixed orange label column and black message column. The message no longer jumps horizontally between pages. All five statements stay on one line with sufficient separation from the label, and their 28px peers have matching apparent weight and height.",
    "All table bodies and headers preserve the24px role. The opening uses a spacious two-column scale table, opportunities uses two denser tables, the operating model uses a responsibility matrix, the roadmap uses a workstream matrix and investment uses two financial tables. Cell wording remains readable within each density.",
    "The roadmap gate evidence now has the same24px annotation level as the other data notes. Corpus/access/signed and Practice lead+CFO/decide fit in three readable lines. The enlarged allocation does not collide with the gate rule or dependency section.",
    "No visible text clipping or object collisions remain in the inspected outputs. The investment implementation qualification clears its lower divider. The opportunity calculation remains entirely above its decision band. The operating-model feedback loops and roadmap dependency arrows remain continuous and visible.",
    "Orange conveys emphasized data, actions and connectors throughout. Black table headers, neutral row fills and the shared pale-orange decision treatment remain consistent. The inherited company header and illustrative-data footer retain the same visible placement and treatment on every page."
